tan nibadhnāti bhārata\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3872,\"bb\":3408,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/8/b3408/\",\"shadow_value\":\"tamaḥ – the mode of ignorance; tu – but; ajñāna-jam – produced of ignorance; viddhi – know; mohanam – the delusion; sarva-dehinām – of all embodied beings; pramāda – with madness; ālasya – indolence; nidrābhiḥ – and sleep; tat – that; nibadhnāti – binds; bhārata – O son of Bharata.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"tamaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the mode of ignorance\"},{\"word\":\"tu\",\"translation\":\"but\"},{\"word\":\"ajñāna-jam\",\"translation\":\"produced of ignorance\"},{\"word\":\"viddhi\",\"translation\":\"know\"},{\"word\":\"mohanam\",\"translation\":\"the delusion\"},{\"word\":\"sarva-dehinām\",\"translation\":\"of all embodied beings\"},{\"word\":\"pramāda\",\"translation\":\"with madness\"},{\"word\":\"ālasya\",\"translation\":\"indolence\"},{\"word\":\"nidrābhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"and sleep\"},{\"word\":\"tat\",\"translation\":\"that\"},{\"word\":\"nibadhnāti\",\"translation\":\"binds\"},{\"word\":\"bhārata\",\"translation\":\"O son of Bharata\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3873,\"bb\":3409,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/8/b3409/\",\"body_value\":\"O son of Bharata, know that the mode of darkness, born of ignorance, is the delusion of all embodied living entities. The results of this mode are madness, indolence and sleep, which bind the conditioned soul.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3874,\"bb\":3410,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/8/b3410/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 14.8\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 14.8\"},\"locale\":\"en\"