vivṛddhaṁ sattvam ity uta\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3890,\"bb\":3423,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/11/b3423/\",\"shadow_value\":\"sarva-dvāreṣu – in all the gates; dehe asmin – in this body; prakāśaḥ – the quality of illumination; upajāyate – develops; jñānam – knowledge; yadā – when; tadā – at that time; vidyāt – know; vivṛddham – increased; sattvam – the mode of goodness; iti uta – thus it is said.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"sarva-dvāreṣu\",\"translation\":\"in all the gates\"},{\"word\":\"dehe asmin\",\"translation\":\"in this body\"},{\"word\":\"prakāśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the quality of illumination\"},{\"word\":\"upajāyate\",\"translation\":\"develops\"},{\"word\":\"jñānam\",\"translation\":\"knowledge\"},{\"word\":\"yadā\",\"translation\":\"when\"},{\"word\":\"tadā\",\"translation\":\"at that time\"},{\"word\":\"vidyāt\",\"translation\":\"know\"},{\"word\":\"vivṛddham\",\"translation\":\"increased\"},{\"word\":\"sattvam\",\"translation\":\"the mode of goodness\"},{\"word\":\"iti uta\",\"translation\":\"thus it is said\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3891,\"bb\":3424,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/11/b3424/\",\"body_value\":\"The manifestation of the mode of goodness can be experienced when all the gates of the body are illuminated by knowledge.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3892,\"bb\":3425,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/11/b3425/\",\"body_value\":\"There are nine gates in the body: two eyes, two ears, two nostrils, the mouth, the genitals and the anus. When every gate is illuminated by the symptoms of goodness, it should be understood that one has developed the mode of goodness. In 